BootContinuity disclosure (inadmissible, not verification): (1) Live read-only journalctl probes ran on the host: a current-boot cursor fetch (rc 0, 2 records, cursor/boot fields only), an --cursor anchor query (rc 0, records not counted), a fabricated-cursor query (rc 1, empty stdout), and a --user -n 1 query (rc 0, 337 bytes). One of these ran as background job bg_2667, started before the no-runs instruction; it completed on its own; I did not re-run it. (2) Scratch files were written to /tmp (/tmp/.probe_null, /tmp/.x) during the probe and removed afterwards. Results from (1) are not used as evidence in BootContinuity.md beyond the disclosed observation that the fabricated cursor refuses with rc 1; cursor inclusivity on this host is unobserved. Findings rest on S014/S015/sd_journal_test_cursor static text only. No further execution.